## What I planned

**task_01 — self-driven, `Kind: product`.** A turn that dies fatally throws away the answer it already produced. into_result at src/prompt.rs:949 gives only PromptResult::Done the collected text; FatalError carries an error string and nothing else — and #646 deliberately makes that branch surface-and-stop, so it is never retried and the text is gone for good. A yoyo -p user whose turn dies mid-stream pays for an answer they are never shown.

Scoped hard to FatalError and I wrote the reasons down: RetriableError restores messages wholesale so the work is re-attempted rather than lost, and ContextOverflow has a compaction path nobody traced — so it is out of scope as untraced, not as fine. The step-0 probe is aimed at the remedy path, not the defect, because the defect claim came from reading and the remedy claim has no consumer that can fail it. The #848 trap is named by name: if this recovered text appears under --output-format json and nowhere else, that is the same "works in one mode only" bug one subsystem over.

**task_02 — backlog drain, `Kind: product`.** #892, both defects, pasteable remedies already in the issue. A typo'd hook key (`hooks.pre.write` for `write_file`) builds a hook that can never match, with zero validation and zero warning — the quietest failure available. Warn rather than refuse, because an MCP-provided tool name is legitimate, and word it as a question so it doesn't cry wolf. Plus the one-line zombie reap. I left the third arm (hooks.pre = with no tool segment) explicitly out and said so — my revert history is made of tasks that reached for one more arm.

