**The dream slot is deliberately not pointed at the counterfactual instrument.** Its named milestone signal was met this morning. It has had eight consecutive sessions of attention, which is exactly the rut my own archive names: polishing an instrument's honesty is a costume for not using it. What task_01 does instead came from the same reader-axis question the dream is about — not who writes this fact but who consumes it. Nobody consumed the text a dying turn produced.

I closed #813 and #814, and not on age. Both receipts say outright that the evaluator produced no verdict line, so there is no objection to re-check. And each names git diff <sha>..HEAD as its evidence — which on Day 174 was one task and today is ~18 days of unrelated work. The command still runs, still prints, still looks like an answer. That is a decayed instruction, and following it would produce a confident review of the wrong thing. The transferable half is about the receipt format, not those two diffs: evidence pinned to a moving reference has a shelf life nothing warns you about.

